---
description: Symphonica design system rules for this React app
alwaysApply: true
---

When working on UI code, always use the project design system context:

- @docs/design-system/Symphonica_design.md
- @docs/design-system/design_tokens.json

This is a React application using Bootstrap (or React-Bootstrap) as the structural foundation for Symphonica.

Rules:
- Preserve existing React functional patterns and hooks logic.
- Do not rewrite complete screens or large component trees unless explicitly requested.
- Do not introduce new dependencies (libraries) unless explicitly requested.
- Do not introduce new visual styles (CSS/inline-styles) unless explicitly requested.

- Bootstrap is part of the foundation of this design system.
- Reuse Bootstrap utilities and layout structure (Rows, Cols, Containers) whenever possible.
- Extend Bootstrap using Symphonica guidelines and tokens.
- Do not replace Bootstrap with another UI framework (like Tailwind or Material UI).

- Symphonica styles and tokens take precedence over default Bootstrap styles.
- When a Bootstrap style conflicts with Symphonica, follow Symphonica.
- Prefer Symphonica visual rules for typography, spacing, colors, borders, shadows and component behavior.

- Use Symphonica tokens instead of hardcoded CSS values.
- If using CSS-in-JS or Styled Components, map props strictly to @docs/design-system/design_tokens.json
- For icons, strictly follow the Material Icons Outlined mapping defined in @Symphonica_design.md.